#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115024 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66534e01-fdc6-522f-b90a-59a8118bc67b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Complex Root of a Quadratic Equation Given the First Root"}] :question/id #uuid "9cb68d4c-a7a7-5bb8-8905-4bb1ee1dc7e8" :question/math-academy-id "e-5776" :question/problem "A quadratic equation with real coefficients has a root $x=5+4\\textrm{i}$. What is the other root?" :question/worked-solution "We're given that the quadratic equation has real coefficients and that\n\n$$\nx=5+4\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nis a root. Therefore, its complex conjugate\n\n$$\nx=5-4\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nis also a root."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115025 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0db14c2a-b6c3-5550-8ff6-c1a9e2b4ea5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Equation Given an Imaginary Root and Its Leading Coefficient"}] :question/id #uuid "4a2ea20e-6982-541a-90c2-7cb4547a357e" :question/math-academy-id "e-5777" :question/problem "A quadratic equation in the variable $x$ with real coefficients has a root $x=-3\\textrm{i}$. Given that the coefficient of $x^2$ in the equation is $2$, find the equation." :question/worked-solution "Since the quadratic equation has real coefficients and\n\n$$\nx=-3\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nis a root, its conjugate\n\n$$\nx = 3\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nmust also be a root. Therefore, using the zero product property, we can write a quadratic equation with the required roots as follows:\n\n$$\n(x-3\\textrm{i})(x+3\\textrm{i})= 0\n$$\n\nMultiplying out the parentheses and simplifying gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} - (3\\textrm{i})^{2} &= 0 \\\\\nx^{2} - 9(-1) &= 0 \\\\\nx^{2} + 9 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation has roots\n\n$$\nx=\\pm 3\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nbut the coefficient of $x^2$ is not $2$. Therefore, to find the desired equation, we multiply the equation above by $2$. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(x^{2} + 9) &= 0 \\\\\n2x^{2} + 18 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115026 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0236acfd-59d1-5bc8-9e60-1c76ddc536f5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Equation Given a Complex Root and Its Leading Coefficient"}] :question/id #uuid "a6f4c4fe-c7e6-5cde-a2ee-ac25feb97f76" :question/math-academy-id "e-5778" :question/problem "A quadratic equation in the variable $x$ with real coefficients has a root $x=6-8\\textrm{i}$. Given that the coefficient of $x^2$ in the equation is $-1$, find the equation." :question/worked-solution "Since the quadratic equation has real coefficients and\n\n$$\nx=6-8\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nis a root, its conjugate\n\n$$\nx=6+8\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nmust also be a root. Therefore, using the zero product property, we can write a quadratic equation with the required roots as follows:\n\n$$\n\\Bigl(x-(6-8\\textrm{i})\\Bigr)\\Bigl(x-(6+8\\textrm{i})\\Bigr) = 0\n$$\n\nBy expanding the parentheses, we can write the equation in standard form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} - x(6 + 8\\textrm{i}) - x(6 - 8\\textrm{i}) + (6 - 8\\textrm{i})(6 + 8\\textrm{i}) &= 0 \\\\\nx^{2} - 6x - 8x\\textrm{i} - 6x + 8x\\textrm{i} + 36 - 64\\textrm{i}^{2} &= 0 \\\\\nx^{2} - 12x + 36 + 64 &= 0 \\\\\nx^{2} - 12x + 100 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation has roots\n\n$$\nx= 6 \\pm 8\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nbut the coefficient of $x^2$ is not $-1$. Therefore, to find the desired equation, we multiply the equation above by $-1$. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n- (x^{2} - 12x + 100) &= 0 \\\\\n- x^{2} + 12x - 100 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115588 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0236acfd-59d1-5bc8-9e60-1c76ddc536f5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Equation Given a Complex Root and Its Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b65ba28c-241a-52bb-8865-ac4f88d29192" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2} + x - 2 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112929} {:answer/id #uuid "261cf6a9-75c6-576e-aa16-b962a0de2823" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2} - 2x = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112930} {:answer/id #uuid "41be664d-71b0-5226-8974-fc5ae7037fd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2} - x + 1 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112931} {:answer/id #uuid "45e2a6ac-ac5c-5b04-b2e1-b97bbdd3a86c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2} + 2x + 2 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112932} {:answer/id #uuid "6ab86ab2-6d83-5cff-93d2-51aa95e549e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2} + 2 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45e2a6ac-ac5c-5b04-b2e1-b97bbdd3a86c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2} + 2x + 2 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112932} :answer-field/id #uuid "230cf8eb-448c-56e4-a4c8-a98d9a2b5fd8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112928}] :question/id #uuid "8b3e3d2a-46f3-5327-8b01-7846488f9aea" :question/math-academy-id "q-28215" :question/problem "A quadratic equation in the variable $x$ with real coefficients has a root $x =-1 + \\textrm{i}$. Given that the coefficient of $x^{2}$ in the equation is $1$, find the equation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115609 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66534e01-fdc6-522f-b90a-59a8118bc67b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Complex Root of a Quadratic Equation Given the First Root"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd805d20-efbe-5d3f-8f4c-a700bd004c26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113055} {:answer/id #uuid "d95eb18e-4241-5d70-8f9b-19a98387ca20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3 + \\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113056} {:answer/id #uuid "5a8c5e4b-c6ce-5fe2-a1bb-b0443679074b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - 3\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113057} {:answer/id #uuid "6398d19f-2bb5-581b-85f3-7e6a812b7c32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 + \\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113058} {:answer/id #uuid "75ccfac7-80fc-5471-bb71-558ad2e5cf83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + 3\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6398d19f-2bb5-581b-85f3-7e6a812b7c32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 + \\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113058} :answer-field/id #uuid "12d5025f-6e72-5e2d-ad0f-108caae8ca89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113054}] :question/id #uuid "9c748dd1-062a-5866-ad04-0894e90b8522" :question/math-academy-id "q-28502" :question/problem "A quadratic equation with real coefficients has a root $x = 3 - \\textrm{i}$. What is the other root?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115612 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0db14c2a-b6c3-5550-8ff6-c1a9e2b4ea5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Equation Given an Imaginary Root and Its Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af31cb05-1759-5b66-80d6-9f1c252014ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x^{2} - 12 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113073} {:answer/id #uuid "dd9fe814-709a-5981-a8cd-e1d6ef1ce0ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x^{2} - 4 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113074} {:answer/id #uuid "f83b13d2-c942-5f6d-848c-b96b9f52e280" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x^{2} + 6 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113075} {:answer/id #uuid "37840ade-d6f7-53f9-bcd4-90d1ebf43172" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x^{2} + 4 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113